Virat Kohli is an Indian international cricketer and the former all-format captain, widely regarded as one of the greatest batsmen in the history of the game. He is 37 years old as of December 27, 2025, born on November 5, 1988, in Delhi, India. 
Kohli retired from Test cricket in May 2025 but continues to play in ODI and T20 formats, recently becoming the second Indian batter after Sachin Tendulkar to cross the 16,000-run mark in List A cricket. 

Recent Trends and News
List A Record: In a recent Vijay Hazare Trophy match, Kohli scored 77 runs off 61 balls, achieving the highest batting average in List A cricket history, surpassing Michael Bevan's long-standing record.
Upcoming Milestone: He is just 25 runs away from reaching 28,000 international runs, a milestone only Sachin Tendulkar has achieved for India so far.
Net Worth: As of 2025, Virat Kohli's net worth is estimated at around ₹1,050 crore (approximately $126-127 million), making him one of the wealthiest and most marketable athletes in the world. 
